    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "Rocket User’s Manual",
      "notes": "Controller chart (pages 34) read by tools/profiles/waldorf/read-waldorf-cc.mjs from Rocket_Manual.pdf (sha256 9addb3d7e77ac01e565223815b2a09357221c3d0a7098b33a240fe80f8d8f2e4), https://downloads.waldorfmusic.com/cloud/index.php/s/zPyonKEbNXiyiZ6/download (Documentation EN/Rocket_Manual.pdf in the zip). Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/waldorf/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/waldorf/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the manual's controller chart, with its printed name, sent as a control change on the channel variable. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "The Rocket can be switched to an alternative controller assignment by SysEx (its manual's `Alt Ctrl #` column, to drive another Waldorf synthesizer); this profile uses the standard one.",
    "Left out, performance and channel mode controllers, which change no setting of the sound: CC 1 Modulation Wheel, CC 64 Sustain Pedal, CC 120 All Sound Off, CC 121 Reset All Control- lers, CC 122 Local Control, CC 123 All Notes Off."
  ],
